<title>GERMANY: Grundig 1996 loss narrows to 553 mln DM.</title>
<headline>Grundig 1996 loss narrows to 553 mln DM.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996:</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net loss			     553     vs 598</p>
<p>    Group operating loss		     382     vs 288</p>
<p>    Group sales				  3,320   vs 3,500</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German consumer electronics group is Grundig AG. The 1996 business year is the last in which the company's largest shareholder, Philips, is required to compensate Grundig losses.</p>
<p>Christian Schwarz-Schilling, Grundig supervisory board chairman, said the company would be able to survive on its own and predicted it would return to profitability, but did not elaborate.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097 150</p>
</text>
